    {
      "id": "662a708a-aa31-4c65-ac41-977a6154650a",
      "name": "One Protocol, Every Assistant",
      "path": "WWW / Why MCP Is Awesome / One Protocol, Every Assistant",
      "docTypeId": "d3054eb2-9a6c-44cc-bfc9-b5f02379703c",
      "templateId": "d01f27e6-1492-4b1c-b1be-849fcd849c2d",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "One Protocol, Every Assistant"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-08 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "MCP's quiet superpower is that it is boring: a standard JSON contract that any client and any server can speak, so the ecosystem compounds instead of fragmenting."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "listingImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "87eb5461-0179-4996-a955-623597ec934e",
              "mediaKey": "b30da9f9-17b0-4329-b9b0-b871cd793c75",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "9c693991-a7c5-4a81-b417-643a4b69a15e",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "db5dc885-aba7-402d-aae5-96ab324d1a55",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "776f7d4c-9689-44b0-a542-03d1fcd0fc45",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "620f97c9-a1ff-437f-80b8-b3711b997e88",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "b331764d-c903-4f97-a18f-3fe5048b2aed",
                "key": "9c693991-a7c5-4a81-b417-643a4b69a15e",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Plenty of standards fail because they are clever. MCP is succeeding because it is boring: JSON-RPC messages over stdio or HTTP, a small surface of tools, resources and prompts, and versioned capabilities negotiated at startup. Any language, any runtime, any assistant.</p><p>Boring is what lets an ecosystem compound. A server written for one client works on all of them; a client improvement benefits every server at once.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "8a210f7d-d727-487d-ab27-bc14d52a65d1",
                "key": "db5dc885-aba7-402d-aae5-96ab324d1a55",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Photo: Conny Schneider on Unsplash"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "85562064-9ba6-43fb-b358-35fb4424ccd4",
                        "mediaKey": "a63adb88-8508-40e1-a806-716a404cab13",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "b331764d-c903-4f97-a18f-3fe5048b2aed",
                "key": "776f7d4c-9689-44b0-a542-03d1fcd0fc45",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>The compounding is already visible: databases, design tools, browsers and content systems — including this Umbraco site — expose themselves over MCP, and each new server raises the value of every client. No N×M integration matrix, just one protocol each side speaks.</p><p>When you evaluate your next stack, ask one question: can it speak MCP? If yes, it is not just a tool, it is part of the graph.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "f2659879-c11a-4796-9fc6-ce46ce3455be",
                "key": "620f97c9-a1ff-437f-80b8-b3711b997e88",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "attribution",
                    "value": "The Umbraco.Bench blog"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "quote",
                    "value": "A good protocol disappears. MCP's greatest success will be that nobody talks about it — they just use it."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "9c693991-a7c5-4a81-b417-643a4b69a15e",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "db5dc885-aba7-402d-aae5-96ab324d1a55",
